X:1
T:Ffarwel Trwy'r Pwll
T:Farewell through the Puddle (sic)
C:Trad
B:51 Welsh Airs
S:https://trillian.mit.edu/~jc/music/abc/mirror/BrianMartin/msg/ejones.abc
A:Wales
H:From a facsimile c.1840: A Choice Collection of Fifty-One Welsh Airs adapted for The Harp, Piano-Forte, Harpsichord, Violin, or Flute by Edward Jones "Harper to His Late Majesty King George IV, when Prince of Wales".
N:The Welsh word 'pwll' has two meanings; 'pwll glo' is a coal 'mine';
N:'pwll nofio' is a swimming 'pool'.  A puddle is a 'pwllyn'.
N:Another word 'pwyll' means 'sense or discretion'.  I'd be inclined
N:to take (away) the piss and leave discretion behind!  BM.
